{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"degradable-appalling-cavy","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nInvestigation absurd-zoometric-bobwhite measured 238,486,830 logical bytes of active and retired REVIEW_RESULT files in the current tickets tree. REVIEW_RESULT is reducer-ignored and compaction-preserved. The active per-ticket cap is already respected: no ticket has more than 50 active results, so the existing explicit prune would currently remove zero active files, while retired sidecars remain outside that prune. This is intentional observability data rather than the reconciler regression, but it is a first-order contributor to the greater-than-1-GiB checkout.\n\n## Plan\n- Attribute payload bytes by schema field, producer, ticket, active versus retired lifecycle, and analytical consumer.\n- Define the minimum retained material needed for remediation recall, audit, calibration, and gate observability.\n- Design a merge-safe retention/slimming strategy that covers retired as well as active sidecars and remains safe across stale independent clones.\n- Provide a one-time reclaim path and ongoing budget signal with semantic-consumer parity checks.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Current REVIEW_RESULT bytes and their required consumers are quantified.\n- [ ] The design bounds both active and retired sidecar growth without destructive concurrent-clone conflicts.\n- [ ] Required review recall, audit, and calibration outputs remain semantically equivalent.\n- [ ] A fresh-clone before/after measurement reports logical, allocated, and pack savings.\n- [ ] Ongoing growth has an enforceable, portable budget signal.","id":"32d4-9ff7-f582-453f","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["store","llm","retention","review"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Bound and reclaim REVIEW_RESULT sidecar payload growth"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787520831110587001,"uuid":"8ba76f78-3615-4a88-afc2-d35ada2ec256"}